# The web Dockerfile installs from package-lock.json and COPYs only index.html,
# the tsconfigs (including tsconfig.image.json), vite.config.ts, public, src,
# docker/icons and one server script — so nothing below is ever read by a build.
# Without this file the daemon still transfers all of it: ~584 MB of
# node_modules alone, on every build.
#
# CORRECTED 2026-09-04, and the correction is the point. This paragraph used to
# say `server/src` was on that list "because the client's typecheck reaches
# across the package boundary", and that `server/src` "must stay transferable".
# It was never true: no Dockerfile in this repository has ever COPYd
# `server/src`, on any branch — the paragraph described a fix that was
# considered and rejected, in the present tense. The boundary is closed the
# other way round: `tsconfig.image.json` EXCLUDES test files from the image
# typecheck, so the three conformance tests in `src/lib/automerge/` that import
# the server's implementation on purpose are simply not compiled there. They are
# compiled at the repository root, by `npm run build`, in CI and in ci:local.
#
# The one server path the WEB build reads is
# `server/patch-automerge-peer-sync-state.mjs`, named file by file in the
# Dockerfile. `server/node_modules` and `server/dist` stay excluded below.
#
# `server/src` is NOT excluded, and this file no longer claims a reason for
# that: it is simply still transferred, and no stage of the web image reads it.
# Excluding it would cost the API image nothing — that one builds from
# `context: ./server` (compose.maplespire.yml), so this list never applies to
# it — but the saving has not been measured and a merge is not where to find
# out. What this paragraph had to stop doing is describing a COPY that has never
# existed on any branch.
node_modules
server/node_modules
.git
.claude
dist
server/dist
data
reports
.probes
.env
.env.*
server/.env
server/.env.*
test-results
playwright-report
e2e
docs
*.png
*.jpeg
*.jpg
